@page "/samples"

<h3>Sample Files</h3>
<p class="text-muted">
    Try uploading these example files to see how the app processes different formats.
    You can also upload your own receipts or JSON files — these samples are just for demonstration.
</p>

<ul class="list-group">
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <a href="sample-data/receipt.jpg" download>Sample Receipt (Image)</a>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <a href="sample-data/expenses.json" download>Sample Expenses (JSON)</a>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <a href="sample-data/expenses.txt" download>Sample Expenses (Text)</a>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <a href="sample-data/invoice.pdf" download>Sample Invoice (PDF)</a>
    </li>
    <li class="list-group-item">
        <div class="ratio ratio-16x9">
            <p>Sample Demo Video (MP4)</p>
            <video controls>
                <source src="sample-data/ExpenseCategorizer.mp4" type="video/mp4">
                Your browser does not support the video tag.
            </video>
        </div>
               
    </li>
</ul>
